"""layers.1.mlp.down_proj:5850 -- a "san"-sound detector (with a small "than" side effect).

What it does: this component is silent almost everywhere, and when it fires it is mostly
NEGATIVE, on tokens that spell or complete the sound "san":
  - a token that is "san" itself, e.g. " San" (San Diego, San Francisco), " san", "SAN",
    and "Usan"/"Asan"-type pieces: strongly negative;
  - "Sant"/"Santa"/"Santos"-type pieces: moderately negative;
  - the Han characters for san or saint (桑, 聖, 圣): strongly negative;
  - a bare "an"-piece that continues a word ending in "s" or "z" (the "an" of
    "Sus|ana", "Mas|an", "Ahs|an", "Muz|an"), which completes the sound "san":
    strongly negative.
It is weakly POSITIVE on " than" (and on word-internal "than"/"han", more strongly).
It is NEGATIVE on " me" after "Let" ("Let me think"), about -0.85, and weakly negative
on " me" elsewhere. Every other token gets 0.

Why: the variance is dominated by these few token shapes. The rest is small, diffuse,
token-dependent noise that no short rule captures.
"""

READS = ()

SANT_WORDS = {"sant", "santa", "saint", "santo", "santos", "sanit"}
AN_PIECES = {"an", "ana", "ani", "ans", "ano", "anc", "anne", "ant", "ants", "ante"}
SAN_CHARS = {"聖", "圣", "桑"}


def step(carry, prefix, upstream):
    tok = prefix.token_strings[-1]
    word = tok.strip().lower()
    spaced = tok[:1] == " "
    new_doc = len(prefix) == 1 or prefix.document_ids[-2] != prefix.document_ids[-1]
    prev = "" if new_doc else prefix.token_strings[-2].strip().lower()
    if (word.endswith("san") and word != "susan") or tok.strip() in SAN_CHARS:
        value = -4.5
    elif word in SANT_WORDS:
        value = -2.0
    elif not spaced and word in AN_PIECES and prev[-1:] in ("s", "z"):
        value = -5.0
    elif spaced and word == "than":
        value = 0.2
    elif word in ("than", "han"):
        value = 1.8
    elif spaced and word == "me":
        value = -0.85 if prev == "let" else -0.2
    else:
        value = 0.0
    return carry, value

