"""Approximate a few spelling-sensitive responses of this early MLP component.

The clearest negative is the unspaced fragment 'bed', including in 'testbed'.
Ordinary 'be' after an auxiliary is nearly quiet, unlike less usual contexts.
Short be-initial words after 'to' and the re- prefix also get negative values.
Two small positive spelling responses and doubled middle dots are included.
This is a partial lexical explanation, not a general detector of the letter e.
