The negative response covers account/customer words in several languages,
including the Chinese 'household/account' character and Japanese door character.
A root completed across token boundaries is often much stronger than the same
word in one token. Similar c/k + nasal spellings also produce weaker echoes.
Otherwise it predicts zero, except for a positive repeated-interpunct response.
