"""Recognise testing/qualification language and a few formatting cues.

Negative responses mark test-passing prose and educational compounds;
Go's '--- PASS' log marker has the opposite sign. Short text history
separates these uses. Forum labels and document-opening punctuation
have separate, repeatable responses. This is a partial approximation:
unrecognised text receives zero, rather than a token-specific lookup.
