A vowel suffix after s and a small fragment such as se/ase/iser give
negative responses. Double s is weaker. Complete, common words are quieter.
Some analogous syllables in other scripts and document-initial Title:
metadata have separate responses. This is a spelling approximation: it
omits much of the variation between particular words.
